 "era": "-600-400",
 "_about": "A GREEK TEMPLE'S FLORAL ACROTERION, the ornament on a pediment's apex (the Parthenon's, some 4 m tall): from a calyx of acanthus leaves on its plinth two volutes rise in an S and curl in, and a palmette fans out over them -- a fan of spoon-shaped leaves, alternately two colours, round a red heart; painted, as it was, the leaves green, red and blue, the volutes gilt. Its face is the x-y plane (it faces +z and -z alike), `h` its height. (tools: hand-made; arch: a part of `type: item`, the temples' acroteria)",
